eral: \"more than just a hobby\" — it gives him a sense of achievement and purpose [S7T6].\n- Gets \"a real buzz\" transforming something that's not working into something that runs smoothly — \"like giving it a second chance\" [S7T6].\n- Giving something a new life \"makes [him] feel powerful and happy — like [he] really achieved something\"; he agreed with Calvin that they both \"take something and make it look amazing\" [S7T7][S7T8].\n- On 2023-08-03, said fixing cars is like therapy for him; growing up he worked on cars with his dad, and refurbishing them gives him a sense of fulfillment [S12T2].\n- On 2023-09-02, when telling Calvin he's been tied up with car stuff, said fixing stuff up and seeing it turn out better is \"really rewarding and gives me a sense of purpose\", and that fixing someone's car makes him feel like he's \"making a difference\"; he's made \"proud\" to see the relief on someone's face when their car is fixed (echoing his long-stated sense of purpose from fixing things, see above) [S17T3][S17T5].\n- Has fond memories of working on cars with his dad as a kid: they spent one summer restoring an old car — \"It was hard work, but seeing the end result and knowing that we did it together was really satisfying\" [S12T4].\n- Shared a photo from that time: a man and a child (Dave and his dad) posing for a picture — \"a wonderful experience\" [S12T6].\n- On 2023-09-15, told Calvin (answering whether it's satisfying to see his hard work pay off, on the restoration finished that day — context in ## Car mod workshop (2023-08-11)) that \"It's so satisfying to see this brought back to life,\" especially seeing people's reactions when they see the finished product — \"makes all the hard work worth it\" [S19T9].\n- On 2023-10-04, said he loves being able to transform something old and beat-up into something beautiful, and that it's the small successes that make him feel proud and fulfilled (said to Calvin right after Calvin praised his grease-stained hands — \"Those hands show you worked hard. You put in lots of effort. You should definitely be proud!\" — context in ## Car mod workshop (2023-08-11)) [S21T10].","text_sha256":"f6f950c6fb23809aa6b67cd8b70a5d29ead3884f4040c6bc64b3ae7bdf138802","timestamp":null},{"attribution_index_sha256":"98109144a5a23da7a5b89634be2c543ea2366f2abe85f1f3f8a3df64a5e92ce2","attribution_units":[{"dia_ids":["D22:5","D22:6","D22:7"],"kind":"curated_fact","line_end":84,"line_start":84,"source_locators":["[S22T5]","[S22T6]","[S22T7]"],"text_sha256":"16f201ed8c08889fcaf8ab09277f37d04d02ab9abf680fa73bfc6af143f02a79"},{"dia_ids":["D25:7"],"kind":"curated_fact","line_end":85,"line_start":85,"source_locators":["[S25T7]"],"text_sha256":"7dd72fab5b05a1e345fd4bb424cd3df6aff47c46459ba481a4871f19ed5ae37f"},{"dia_ids":["D25:14","D25:15","D25:16","D25:17"],"kind":"curated_fact","line_end":86,"line_start":86,"source_locators":["[S25T14]","[S25T15]","[S25T16]","[S25T17]"],"text_sha256":"ec778a7d513d0e85d117dbcd4f6118a43a90bbe0e964f9446d69f00b677b836d"}],"dia_ids":["D22:5","D22:6","D22:7","D25:7","D25:14","D25:15","D25:16","D25:17"],"evidence_id":"ev-ac9bd239f7b3759d49024f11c9ae89a55a13aa6e9786b37d91dea0a19a54b8c6","group_id":"/memories/dave.md > # Dave","line_end":86,"line_start":84,"observation_ids":["obs-0004"],"path":"/memories/dave.md","query_terms":[],"rank":null,"records_sha256":"130a5a1e1b75083358ef27a98dd215a4e75c819ace6f2ee9b560ba394e0f0394","retrieval_round":5,"schema_version":1,"score":null,"section":"# Dave > ## Hobbies and sense of purpose","selection_ordinal":6,"session_id":null,"source_kind":"curated","source_locators":["[S22T5]","[S22T6]","[S22T7]","[S25T7]","[S25T14]","[S25T15]","[S25T16]","[S25T17]"],"source_map_sha256":"6e99115961bae06a48bfb7e82dbdcc18dc32ccf6c5ce57e3c266dfc7a5d4d574","source_records":[{"dia_id":"D22:5","global_turn_index":374,"locator":"[S22T5]","raw_turn_sha256":"d9df745e960a9235c8ef6144815906d4e022abaaa2b260446481c487ba842026","rendered_turn_sha256":"1a4bb4e5e3813ac263f8