cars \"can be a real escape from reality\" (he understands the feeling), and that \"doing what you love for a living, that's the ultimate goal,\" adding \"Keep going with it, it's really inspiring.\" [S22T5][S22T6][S22T7].\n- On 2023-10-23, told Calvin he recently had a good conversation with some neighbors about current events and politics — it was nice to hear different perspectives and share their own; he finds that interacting like that cheers him up and helps him stay informed (conversation flow in the 2023-10-23 entry of ## Relationships; Calvin's response in the Music and Relationships sections of /memories/calvin.md) [S25T7].\n- On 2023-10-23, told Calvin (who asked \"what made you start working on cars?\") that his car passion started when he was ten: he'd been fascinated with how machines work, found an old car in a neighbor's garage, and asked if he could fix it — \"that's when my love for car engineering began!\" — he enjoyed transforming it from broken-down to high-running, and that sense of accomplishment made him hooked, so he's been working on cars ever since (shared a photo of a man working on a car in a garage; comes with his remark that working on a car is his outlet — \"a little oasis of calm\" — where he's \"connecting back with myself\" — see the 2023-10-23 entry of ## Relationships; complements the childhood memories of tinkering with engines in his dad's garage recorded above; Calvin: \"Impressive! That must have taken a lot of skill and determination to bring that car back to life.\", and asked whether it was a classic car and whether Dave still has it or is working on another project — Dave answered in the continuation of the same day's chat, which is not in this excerpt: he restored a car last year (2022, the 2022 restoration, see above) but sold it to a collector, and is now working on a new car project he finds quite a challenge [S25T14][S25T15][S25T16][S25T17].","text_sha256":"526cdbed8d80172f847714aff975926d5b3e2481d58ce442e90aadc38780